WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Controls and thermostats are the brain of the system. When they fail, nothing
works right.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Leak detection lab: practice using electronic leak detectors, UV dye systems,
soap bubbles, and nitrogen pressure testing on systems with known leaks. Learn
to systematically check common leak points: service valve cores, flare

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Finding leaks efficiently saves time and
money. Systematic checking of common leak points is faster than random
searching.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Watch out for these: Check service valve cores first — most common leak point.
And — Electronic detectors must be calibrated before use

00:02:24.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

